-- gambas-asn1#422 review: exercises the SEQUENCE OF/SET OF stub_reason path
-- (RustBackend.cpp's sequence_member_covered) for a wide-range INTEGER
-- element. Unlike a member-level wide INTEGER (storage_kind intercepted by
-- rust_tag_for_builtin_or_alias, always covered — see rust_wide_types_test.asn1),
-- a SEQUENCE OF/SET OF element's coverage check calls builtin_ber_tag directly
-- with no storage_kind interception (Generator::classify_integer_storage only
-- runs per-member, not per-element) — its Integer case only accepts
-- mtype == "i64", so a semi-constrained non-negative element (u64 storage,
-- X.680 semi-constrained INTEGER, `0..MAX`) makes this member land in
-- MemberAccess::Unsupported rather than getting a real encode/decode row —
-- a real, currently-untested coverage gap (large-integer SEQUENCE OF/SET OF
-- element support), not dead code.

RustSeqOfWideIntTest DEFINITIONS ::= BEGIN

    WideIntList ::= SEQUENCE {
        counts SEQUENCE OF INTEGER (0..MAX)
    }

END
